XnuPrelink 440589b (+ fixture and local-relocation patches): PAC layouts for a plain arm64 native kernel

vtable_slots() only accepted IA-signed slots, so no table of the arm64 NABU
kernel was ever recognised (0 vtable binds). A no-PAC native table now borrows
the complete PAC layout of the same-named __ZTV table in the symbol-bearing
arm64e reference (VMAPPLE, same XNU 12377 sources). The table must end at the
same slot count and carry one unambiguous name, otherwise it is skipped, so the
slot-by-slot layout comparison keeps its strength.

Run 23 + macOS 27.3: 860 vtable binds, kext-facing targets named 1635 -> 1958,
strict APFS emission unresolved references 7455 -> 1001. 73 tests OK.
